     An `@page` margin was here and the first line still printed against the
     edge. The rule is in the built stylesheet and the stylesheet is served —
     so the rule is not the thing that failed. What can still override it is
     the browser: Chrome remembers the margin setting from whatever was
     printed last, and `More settings -> Margins -> None` wins over any
     stylesheet.
  
     So the two edges are held differently. Top and bottom stay in `@page`,
     because only a page margin repeats on every sheet — padding on a block
     applies once at its start and once at its end, and the middle pages of a
     six page notebook would have neither.
  
